# App icons

## Two tracks (do not mix)

| Kind | Source | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Brand / product logos** | [Simple Icons](https://simpleicons.org) | `app/constants/brandIcons.ts` → `BrandIcon.vue` |
| **UI chrome** (expand, close, chevrons, …) | **[Lucide](https://lucide.dev)** (`lucide-vue-next`) | `app/components/icons/Icon*.vue` thin wrappers |

Simple Icons is **brand-only** — never use it for expand/close/menu glyphs.

## UI icons (Lucide)

1. **Package:** `lucide-vue-next` (already in `package.json`).
2. **Naming:** keep `Icon{Name}.vue` in `app/components/icons/` — one Lucide glyph per file (e.g. `IconExpand` → `Maximize2`, `IconMinimize` → `Minimize2`, `IconX` → `X`).
3. **Stroke:** `UI_ICON_STROKE` in `uiIconDefaults.ts` (currently `2`).
4. **Usage:** `<IconExpand class="h-4 w-4" />` — size via Tailwind; color via `currentColor` / parent `text-*`.
5. **New basic icon?** Pick from [lucide.dev/icons](https://lucide.dev/icons), add wrapper `IconFoo.vue`; do not paste raw SVG in pages.
6. **Accessibility:** decorative → `aria-hidden` on wrapper; controls → `aria-label` on the button.

## Brand icons

Follow `provider-brand-icon` skill → `brandIcons.ts`, not Lucide.

## Legacy

`AppIcon.vue` remains for one-off custom SVGs only if Lucide has no match; prefer Lucide for standard UI.